rplane Mode, but my status bar now says “No Signal” and I still don’t see any signal bars. What should I try next?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":35,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:26:36.105904","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":35,"usage":{"completion_tokens":36,"prompt_tokens":3040}},{"content":"Thank you for turning off Airplane Mode. Since you’re still seeing “No Signal,” the next step is to check your SIM card status. Please check if your phone shows any messages about the SIM card (such as “SIM missing” or “SIM locked”), or if it appears to be recognized by your device.\n\nIf you’re not sure how to check your SIM card status, let me know and I can guide you through the process. If your SIM card is not recognized or is missing, try removing it and reinserting it to ensure it’s properly seated. If it’s locked, you may need to contact technical support for further assistance.\n\nLet me know what you find, or if you need step-by-step instructions.","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":36,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:26:38.429961","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":36,"usage":{"completion_tokens":148,"prompt_tokens":8410}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":37,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:26:39.482581","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{},"id":"call_68YeDYPg7LpNwtGqXbz9uRbp","name":"check_sim_status","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":37,"usage":{"completion_tokens":12,"prompt_tokens":3228}},{"content":"No SIM card detected in the phone.","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":38,"